provider: ollama-cloud (glm-5.3)
request: Rename Todo.done to Todo.completed everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> types, commands, format, storage  (Pure rename of the Todo.done field to Todo.completed. The Todo interface is owned by types, and commands, format, and storage all consume it, so all four must switch their references in the same round — including the persisted JSON key in storage. ListOptions.includeDone and the Command type are not Todo.done and stay untouched. Acceptance tests pin the new field name and the on-disk key.)
round 1: owners types=rejected commands=rejected format=rejected storage=rejected; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> types, commands, format, storage  (Round 1 was rejected only because each owner's required test edits awaited approval; those edits are exactly what this rename demands, so I approve all four titles and re-issue the same plan.)
round 2: owners types=ok commands=ok format=ok storage=fail; oracle RED
governor turn 3: plan -> storage  (Only storage is implicated: its last submission was not applied (owner run error), leaving one tsc error in src/storage.test.ts where a todo literal still uses the old `done` field. types, commands, and format are green. Re-instructing storage with the previously requested test change approved.)
round 3: owners storage=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 4: accept  (Rename of Todo.done to Todo.completed is complete across all units: types exports `completed: boolean`, and commands/format/storage all use the new field name. Oracle is green (tsc exit 0, 15/15 tests pass), and the acceptance tests verify the new field name end-to-end, including storage persisting the `completed` JSON key with no `done` key.)

